1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:03,790
Everyone says Ravan was Shiva's greatest devotee.

2
00:00:03,790 --> 00:00:04,291
Really?

3
00:00:04,291 --> 00:00:08,660
This story was narrated by Sage Agastya himself to Lord Rama.

4
00:00:09,330 --> 00:00:10,589
After slaying Ravan,

5
00:00:10,589 --> 00:00:14,430
The name Ravan means the one who makes all three worlds weep.

6
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:18,831
And this name was given to him by Shiva himself.

7
00:00:18,831 --> 00:00:20,949
But back then, he was Dashagriva.

8
00:00:20,949 --> 00:00:23,580
His brother Kuber was a devotee of Shiva.

9
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:25,180
And this used to bother Ravan.

10
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:27,275
After defeating Kuber,

11
00:00:27,275 --> 00:00:29,461
as he was flying in Pushpak Viman,

12
00:00:29,461 --> 00:00:32,355
his chariot suddenly stopped atop a mountain.

13
00:00:32,355 --> 00:00:33,770
Turn back, Dashagriva.

14
00:00:33,870 --> 00:00:36,722
Lord Shankar resides on this mountain.

15
00:00:36,722 --> 00:00:37,623
Shankar who?

16
00:00:37,623 --> 00:00:40,100
I will uproot this very mountain.

17
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:44,940
Mahadev simply pressed down with his big toe,

18
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:48,191
and all three worlds trembled.

19
00:00:48,191 --> 00:00:50,180
Upon his ministers' advice,

20
00:00:50,310 --> 00:00:54,099
he wept in pain from his crushed arms for a thousand years,

21
00:00:54,099 --> 00:00:55,640
singing hymns of praise.

22
00:00:56,490 --> 00:01:00,410
[Sanskrit] Because the three worlds were made to cry and tremble by you,

23
00:01:01,260 --> 00:01:02,905
[Sanskrit] therefore O king,

24
00:01:02,905 --> 00:01:05,020
your name shall henceforth be Ravan.

25
00:01:05,870 --> 00:01:07,775
Ravan, the terror of the worlds.

26
00:01:07,775 --> 00:01:09,620
You made all three worlds weep.

27
00:01:11,730 --> 00:01:14,250
Therefore, from today your name

28
00:01:14,370 --> 00:01:14,980
is Ravan.

29
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:17,602
After that, Valmiki writes,

30
00:01:17,602 --> 00:01:18,712
wherever he went,

31
00:01:18,712 --> 00:01:21,780
a golden Shiva linga would travel ahead of him.

32
00:01:23,870 --> 00:01:26,505
He who once asked, 'Who is Shankar?',

33
00:01:26,505 --> 00:01:29,638
now bowed before the Shiva linga everywhere.

34
00:01:29,638 --> 00:01:30,920
Was this devotion,

35
00:01:31,370 --> 00:01:32,500
or the fear of that toe?

36
00:01:34,250 --> 00:01:36,520
More secrets of Ravan in the next story.

